\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\lang1040\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. THIS is the day of light:
\par Let there be light to-day;
\par O Day-spring, rise upon our night,
\par And chase its gloom away.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. This is the day of rest:
\par Our falling strength renew;
\par On weary brain and troubled breast
\par Shed Thou Thy freshening dew.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. This is the day of peace:
\par Thy peace our spirits filled
\par Bid thou the blasts of discord cease,
\par The waves of strife be still.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. This is the day of prayer:
\par Let earth to heaven draw near;
\par Lift up our hearts to seek Thee there,
\par Come down to meet us here.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. This is the first of days:
\par Send forth Thy quickening breath,
\par And wake dead souls to love and praise,
\par O Vanquisher of death!    
\par                        AMEN.,
\par \lang1033\f1 
\par \cf1\lang1040\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

